packages/blk-wmt: the loader and launcher sequence follows mtk-wmt-init.c from
https://github.com/snowopsdev/omarchy-iplay50-mini-pro (b7fa1570, GPL-2.0). Ioctl numbers and the patch info layouts
follow MediaTek's WMT driver (wmt_detect.h, wmt_dev.c, wmt_lib.h, GPL-2.0) as published in
https://github.com/MotorolaMobilityLLC/vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-common (android-15-release-vvob35,
2993f4be). The NVRAM and Wi-Fi power on writes follow MediaTek's wmt_cdev_wifi.c (GPL-2.0, Dual BSD/GPL module) as
published in https://github.com/MotorolaMobilityLLC/vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-wlan-adaptor
(android-15-release-vvob35, 11353556).
packages/blk-bt: written from MediaTek's stp_chrdev_bt.c (Dual BSD/GPL) as published in
https://github.com/MotorolaMobilityLLC/vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-bt-mt66xx (2a851b31), the Linux
hci_ldisc and hci_h4 drivers and the Bluetooth Core specification. The firmware quirks it handles (the Read
Synchronization Train Parameters reply, the LE command bits in Read Local Supported Commands, the BD address write
after HCI Reset) were found by https://github.com/snowopsdev/omarchy-iplay50-mini-pro (b7fa1570),
https://github.com/Barley-Project/tb330fu-ubuntu (684d207f) and https://github.com/HuskerMinion/techo5 (2fa63874).
packages/bootc: Fedora's bootc 1.17.1-1.fc44 source RPM (https://github.com/bootc-dev/bootc, Apache-2.0 or MIT),
rebuilt with ipc-ns-not-found.patch.
packages/ostree: Fedora's ostree 2026.4-1.fc44 source RPM (https://github.com/ostreedev/ostree, LGPL-2.0-or-later),
rebuilt with selinux-disabled-skip.patch.
packages/waydroid: Fedora's waydroid 1.6.3-1.fc44 source RPM (https://github.com/waydroid/waydroid, GPL-3.0-only),
rebuilt without mount-secontext.patch and the D-Bus activation file, with namespaces-includes.patch,
no-debugfs-bind.patch, net-filter-ipforward.patch, lxc-debug-log.patch, container-session.patch and dbus-policy.patch.
packages/retroarch: Fedora's retroarch 1.22.0-20.fc44 source RPM (https://github.com/libretro/RetroArch,
GPL-3.0-or-later), rebuilt for GLES with gles-context.patch, upstream RetroArch commit db91cdbf (#18436), and
with volume-cap.patch, which stops its volume, mixer volume and mixer stream volumes at 0 dB.
packages/libretro-snes9x: Snes9x (https://github.com/libretro/snes9x, fae2fea, the Snes9x licence: non commercial
use, with LGPL-2.1-or-later and MIT components; the texts under /usr/share/licenses/libretro-snes9x/), built unchanged
as the libretro core.
packages/libretro-genesis-plus-gx: Genesis Plus GX (https://github.com/libretro/Genesis-Plus-GX, f27655b, its own
non commercial licence with LGPL-2.1-or-later and other component licences; the texts under
/usr/share/licenses/libretro-genesis-plus-gx/), built unchanged as the libretro core.
packages/libretro-mupen64plus-next: Mupen64Plus-Next (https://github.com/libretro/mupen64plus-libretro-nx, 15bada8,
GPL-2.0-only with BSD, MIT, zlib and libpng licensed components; the texts under
/usr/share/licenses/libretro-mupen64plus-next/), built with GLideN64 on GLES 3 and no-graphicbuffer.patch, which
excludes GLideN64/src/Graphics/OpenGLContext/GraphicBuffer/PrivateApi/GraphicBuffer.cpp (Android only,
GPL-3.0-or-later) from the Linux build.
packages/libretro-ppsspp: PPSSPP (https://github.com/hrydgard/ppsspp, v1.20.4 fa50bb1, GPL-2.0-or-later with the
component licences under /usr/share/licenses/libretro-ppsspp/), built unchanged as the libretro core, linked static
with FFmpeg (https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg, n7.1.5 3a0867c, LGPL-2.1-or-later) built with only the PSP decoders.
SFMT-LICENSE.txt is SFMT's LICENSE.txt (https://github.com/MersenneTwister-Lab/SFMT, d69c917), which the vendored
ext/sfmt19937 refers to. The assets/flash0/font files were made from Ume and Source Han Sans fonts:
flash0-font-NOTICE.txt records their origin, UmeFont-license.html is license.html of the Ume font 670 release
(umefont_670.tar.xz, as kept by Fedora's horai-ume-fonts) and SourceHanSans-LICENSE.txt is LICENSE.txt of
https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-han-sans (2.001R).
packages/libretro-flycast: Flycast (https://github.com/flyinghead/flycast, v2.7 5aa091f, GPL-2.0-or-later with the
component licences under /usr/share/licenses/libretro-flycast/), built as the libretro core with the version string
set to v2.7. md5-LICENSE is the LICENSE of https://github.com/ulwanski/md5 (bca18c2), where core/deps/md5 comes from.
packages/libretro-shaders-blockie: GLSL shaders from https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders (1aaabbe), unchanged at
their upstream paths: crt/shaders/crt-gdv-mini.glsl (CRT - Guest mini, guest(r) 2017-2018, edited by metallic77,
GPL-2.0-or-later), handheld/shaders/lcd3x.glsl (Gigaherz, public domain), handheld/shaders/zfast_lcd.glsl (Greg Hogan
(SoltanGris42) 2017, GPL-2.0-or-later), handheld/shaders/lcd1x.glsl (Gigaherz's lcd3x edited by jdgleaver,
GPL-2.0-or-later), handheld/shaders/sameboy-lcd.glsl (LIJI32, Lior Halphon 2015-2016, MIT) and
handheld/shaders/retro-v2.glsl (Hyllian 2013, GPL-2.0-or-later). sp101-color.glsl is ported from
handheld/shaders/color/sp101-color.slang of https://github.com/libretro/slang-shaders (afb1416b) by Pokefan531,
hunterk and crashGG (public domain).
packages/gptokeyb: gptokeyb (https://github.com/PortsMaster/gptokeyb, 5b1284e, GPL-2.0-or-later), built with
no-kill-mode.patch, which removes the hotkey plus START kill. The source and the patch are under
/usr/share/blockie/sources/portmaster/gptokeyb/.
packages/gptokeyb2: gptokeyb2 and libinterpose (https://github.com/PortsMaster/gptokeyb2, 647b46f,
GPL-2.0-or-later, with inih under BSD-3-Clause), built with no-kill-mode.patch, which removes the hotkey plus START
kill. The source and the patch are under /usr/share/blockie/sources/portmaster/gptokeyb2/.
packages/libjpeg8: libjpeg-turbo (https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo, 3.1.3 release tarball, IJG,
BSD-3-Clause and Zlib, the texts in LICENSE.md and README.ijg under /usr/share/licenses/libjpeg8/), built with the
libjpeg 8 ABI into /usr/lib64/blockie-ports/compat for Westonpack.
packages/portmaster: PortMaster (https://github.com/PortsMaster/PortMaster-GUI, 2026.11.12-1059 9efc198, MIT, Copyright
(c) 2023-2025 Jacob): the port script helpers and harbourmaster with the libraries it imports, ansimarkup and colorama
